420 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/A 1786 0 R/Alt(The diagram shows the fmi adaptor node architecture, provided by the fmi adaptor package, with three main components. On the left, the fmi adaptor node includes two Subscriber elements, each connected by an arrow to the FMIAdapter. Below these, a Timer element with a clock icon is connected by an arrow to the doStepsUntil function within FMIAdapter. Two Publisher elements are connected by arrows from the getOutputValue function in FMIAdapter. The FMIAdapter, a C plus plus class in the fmi adaptor package, contains functions getAllVariables, setInputValue, doStepsUntil, and getOutputValue. getAllVariables connects to fmi2 get variable in the FMI Library. setInputValue connects to fmi2 set real. doStepsUntil connects to fmi2 do step, with a loop arrow indicating running FMU simulation with given step size. getOutputValue connects to fmi2 get real. The FMI Library, from jmodelica.org slash FMILibrary, contains fmi2 get variable, fmi2 set real, fmi2 do step, and fmi2 get real. A Param colon underscore fmu path connects to Ctor colon path colon string, which then connects to create underscore dllfmu, all leading to the FMI Library. The FMI Library connects to the Application FMU, a zip file with shared library and XML based description of input variables, output variables, and parameters.)/K 22/P 46 0 R/Pg 14 0 R/S/Figure>>
endobj

