<</Type/StructElem/A 1796 0 R/Alt(The diagram illustrates FMI integration in ROS within an Application node. On the left, Subscriber s, Timer s, and Publisher s connect to Application code. The Application code interacts with the FMIAdapter, a C plus plus class in the fmi adaptor package. The FMIAdapter has methods: getAllVariables, setInputValue, doStepsUntil, and getOutputValue. The setInputValue method receives timestamped input values. The doStepsUntil method runs FMU simulation with given step-size, indicated by a curved arrow looping back to itself. The FMIAdapter interacts with the FMI Library, which provides functions like fmi2 get variable, fmi2 set real, fmi2 do step, and fmi2 get real. A path to FMU file leads to Ctor: path: string, which then leads to create dllfmu, which then leads to the FMI Library. The FMI Library and FMIAdapter interact with an Application FMU, described as a zip file with shared library and XML-based description of input variables, output variables, and parameters.)/K 17/P 46 0 R/Pg 15 0 R/S/Figure>>
endobj

