<</Type/StructElem/A 1830 0 R/Alt(The flowchart illustrates a software architecture. At the top, three rectangular nodes are arranged horizontally. From left to right, these are: Model-Based Components, FMU-encapsulated functions; AI-Based Components, ONNX-deployed learned functions; and Robot or Simulator Interfaces, Sensors and actuators. A downward arrow extends from the bottom of each of these three top nodes, converging to point to a single, wider rectangular node below. This node is labelled ROS 2 Nodes slash Wrappers, with the text Data contracts, scheduling, buffering, and orchestration below it. A downward arrow extends from the bottom of the ROS 2 Nodes slash Wrappers node, pointing to another wider rectangular node below. This node is labelled ROS 2 Middleware. Finally, a downward arrow extends from the bottom of the ROS 2 Middleware node, pointing to the bottommost rectangular node, labelled Operating System slash Deployment Platform.)/K 21/P 46 0 R/Pg 18 0 R/S/Figure>>
