898 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/A 1937 0 R/Alt(The line graph displays Yaw Angle in radians on the vertical axis from minus 0.5 to 2, against Time Steps on the horizontal axis from 0 to 400. Two lines are plotted: Original Model and FMU ROS2. Both lines show a similar pattern, starting near 0, rising to approximately 1.5 radians, then decreasing to about minus 0.3 radians, and rising again to approximately 1.6 radians. The FMU ROS2 line closely follows the Original Model line throughout the graph. An inset magnifies a region of the graph from Time Steps 211 to 219 and Yaw Angle 1.43 to 1.61. In this inset, the Original Model line decreases from approximately 1.58 to 1.43, then increases to 1.6. The FMU ROS2 line closely tracks the Original Model line, showing near perfect agreement in this transition region.)/K 15/P 46 0 R/Pg 30 0 R/S/Figure>>
endobj

