913 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/A 1945 0 R/Alt(The line graph displays two curves, Original Model and ONNX ROS2, plotted against Time Step on the horizontal axis and Value on the vertical axis. The Original Model curve, shown in blue, and the ONNX ROS2 curve, shown in orange, largely overlap. Both curves start at a Value of approximately 50, rise sharply to a peak near 220 at Time Step 50, then drop to 0. They remain at 0 until Time Step 125, where they rise to a Value of approximately 45, then drop again to 0 at Time Step 150. The curves then remain at 0 until Time Step 200, where they begin to rise steadily, reaching a peak near 215 at Time Step 375, before declining to a Value of approximately 10 at Time Step 400. An inset graph magnifies the segment from Time Step 170 to 180 on the horizontal axis and Value 185 to 210 on the vertical axis. In the inset, the Original Model curve shows a step-like increase from 185 to 200, then a sharp rise to 210. The ONNX ROS2 curve closely follows the Original Model, showing minimal deviation.)/K 18/P 46 0 R/Pg 31 0 R/S/Figure>>
