<</Type/StructElem/A 1957 0 R/Alt(The two-panel diagram shows a robot trajectory. Panel a is an X-Y position plot of the trajectory. The horizontal axis ranges from 0 to 4 in increments of 0.5. The vertical axis ranges from 0 to 4 in increments of 0.5. A thick orange line starts near the origin, moves right, then sharply up, then right, then up, then right, then up, then right, ending at approximately 3.75 on the horizontal axis and 3.75 on the vertical axis. Panel b shows the trajectory overlaid on a Gazebo map. The map is a grey maze-like environment with black walls. A red circle labelled A is at the bottom left. A red circle labelled B is at the top right. A thick orange line, representing the trajectory, starts at A, navigates through the maze, and ends at B. The path includes several turns and segments that follow the maze corridors.)/K 34/P 46 0 R/Pg 32 0 R/S/Figure>>
